### _U_dyn_cancel

Source: https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/main/src/native/external/libunwind/doc/_U_dyn_cancel.tex

Cancels the registration of unwind info for a dynamically generated procedure. Takes a pointer to the unw_dyn_info_t structure describing the procedure's unwind-info.

```APIDOC
## _U_dyn_cancel

### Description
Cancels the registration of the unwind info for a dynamically generated procedure. The routine is guaranteed to execute in constant time (in the absence of contention from concurrent calls to _U_dyn_register() or _U_dyn_cancel()).

### Syntax
void _U_dyn_cancel(unw_dyn_info_t *di);

### Parameters
- **di** (unw_dyn_info_t *) - Required - Pointer to the unw_dyn_info_t structure that describes the procedure's unwind-info.

### Thread and Signal Safety
_U_dyn_cancel() is thread safe but *not* safe to use from a signal handler.

### See Also
libunwind-dynamic(3libunwind), _U_dyn_register(3libunwind)
```

