### Async continuation context capture with custom awaitable

Source: https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/main/docs/design/coreclr/jit/runtime-async-inlining.md

Shows how async continuations capture synchronization contexts at each await point. The custom awaitable AlwaysThreadPoolAwaitable always suspends and resumes on a thread pool thread, so no context is captured for it. On resumption, the async infrastructure runs Baz directly, then switches to _syncContext2 for Bar's continuation, then to _syncContext1 for Foo's continuation.

```csharp
public static async Task Foo()
{
    SynchronizationContext.SetSynchronizationContext(_syncContext1);
    await Bar();
}

private static async Task Bar()
{
    SynchronizationContext.SetSynchronizationContext(_syncContext2);
    await Baz();
}

private static async Task Baz()
{
    await new AlwaysThreadPoolAwaitable();
}

private struct AlwaysThreadPoolAwaitable : INotifyCompletion
{
    public bool IsCompleted => false;
    public void OnCompleted(Action continuation)
    {
        ThreadPool.QueueUserWorkItem(_ => { Thread.Sleep(100); continuation(); });
    }
    public void GetResult() { }

    public AlwaysThreadPoolAwaitable GetAwaiter() => this;
}
```

