### Switch context for inlined async continuation

Source: https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/main/docs/design/coreclr/jit/runtime-async-inlining.md

Ensures the continuation runs on the proper synchronization context. If not on the right context, it suspends, switches, and resumes via AsyncHelpers.SwitchContext. IsOnRightContext is expected to be true almost always.

```csharp
if (resumed_C && !AsyncHelpers.IsOnRightContext(continuation.ContinuationContextForB, continuation.FlagsForB))
  await AsyncHelpers.SwitchContext(continuation.ContinuationContextForB, continuation.FlagsForB);
