### Create logs with ILogger<T> in Worker

Source: https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/main/src/libraries/Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions/src/PACKAGE.md

Shows a Worker class that uses ILogger<T> to log information. The ExecuteAsync method logs a message with a timestamp and delays one second between iterations until cancellation is requested.

```C#
// Worker class that uses logger implementation of teh interface ILogger<T>

public sealed class Worker : BackgroundService
{
    private readonly ILogger<Worker> _logger;

    public Worker(ILogger<Worker> logger) =>
        _logger = logger;

    protected override async Task ExecuteAsync(CancellationToken stoppingToken)
    {
        while (!stoppingToken.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            _logger.LogInformation("Worker running at: {time}", DateTimeOffset.UtcNow);
            await Task.Delay(1_000, stoppingToken);
        }
    }
}

```

